      "role": "user",
      "content": "I think I follow. So it's basically just the inevitable unpredictability of the data itself. When I'm writing this up, I want to make sure I don't make it sound like the error is a \"fault\" in my study, but just a natural part of the process. Is there a good way to articulate how this \"noise\" or \"uncertainty\" can sometimes obscure the true patterns we're looking for?",
